# Keep shell scripts LF-only so they stay runnable after a clone on
# Linux/macOS/WSL, regardless of the committer's platform or core.autocrlf.
#
# Not theoretical here: tests/run-tests.sh is what CI's Debian leg runs, and a
# `\r` at the end of its shebang or of any `then`/`fi` line makes sh fail in
# ways that read as a broken script rather than a line-ending problem. The
# working copies of redo.sh and the .ps1 files are already CRLF on this machine,
# which is exactly how it would get in.
*.sh text eol=lf
